{
 "id": "flanger-names",
 "version": "0.2",
 "title": "Flanger names (FL01)",
 "category": "Examples",
 "license": "GPL-2.0-or-later",
 "author": "naturarum",
 "description": "For dn2-cfw's FL01 build, whose DSP runs a flanger in the chorus slot (its knob C is TIME, the centre delay, from a phaser-like 0.05 ms through the flanger to a 25.7 ms chorus) and the stock delay in the delay slot: renames the chorus page and every chorus send to Flanger/FLG, and the chorus page's knob C from High-pass/HPF to Time/TIME, with a new-kit default of 32 (the flanger of earlier builds); every delay name stays stock. 0.1 (CMP4) is the same without the knob C sites. Labels and one default only: no new rows, knobs or glyphs, and every knob keeps its MIDI CC, storage and DSP frame word. On a stock DSP the chorus would be named Flanger and its HPF knob Time.",
 "device": "digitone-mk2",
 "os": "1.12",
